# Dynamic Reservation-Driven Equipment Allocation

This plan completely eliminates the hardcoded `ALLOC_RULES` and shifts the allocation engine to be 100% driven by the data in your database and the selected reservation.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **This requires one final SQL script.**
> To permanently remove the hardcoded rules, your Supabase database needs to know *how* to calculate quantities for each item (e.g., 1 per pax, 1 per 8 pax, flat 4). We will add `rule_type` and `rule_ratio` columns directly to your `equipment_inventory` table. This way, every single equipment you ever add will carry its own unique math rule forever.

## Open Questions

None at this time. If you approve this plan, I will provide the SQL script and immediately implement the JavaScript changes.

## Proposed Changes

### Supabase Database Update
- Provide a `.sql` script to add `rule_type` and `rule_ratio` to the `equipment_inventory` table.
- The script will automatically backfill the correct mathematical ratios for your existing items (e.g., Tables = per_table ratio 1.0, Plates = per_pax ratio 1.0).

### JavaScript Architecture (`admin.js`)
- **[MODIFY] Add Equipment Modal:** Update `submitAddEquipment` so that the Rule Type and Ratio you select in the UI are permanently saved directly to the new Supabase columns.
- **[MODIFY] Load Engine:** Update `loadEIMFromSupabase` to pull the new `rule_type` and `rule_ratio` fields.
- **[MODIFY] Allocation Engine (`_showEquipmentNeededList` & `generateAllocationManifest`):**
  - Delete the hardcoded `ALLOC_RULES` loop.
  - Instead, the engine will loop directly through the `packageItems` inside the selected reservation.
  - For each equipment item in the reservation package, it will look up the item in Supabase, grab its dynamic rule, and compute exactly how many you need (Pax × Ratio, etc.).

